ABL="Ableton/MIDI-friendly: every part is a MIDI clip derived from one progression clip; voicings are explicit MIDI notes."
EARLY="If the track has drums, they enter early (~8 counts / ~12 s); only pad/texture before that (Matt's preference)."

S("ET1CvImwzxw","How I Turned 1 Chord Into a Hypnotic, Melodic Ambient Track",
 "one-progression-to-ambient-layers-parallel-maj7-bass-root-split-upper-voicing-octave-tighten-common-tone-root-4-5-arp-seconds-dyad-pad-anticipated-melody-octave-double-long-attack-swells",
 "Turn one chord progression into a full set of ambient layers: parallel maj7 progression (e.g. Cmaj7-Gmaj7-Bbmaj7-Fmaj7, 4 bars of long sustained chords) copied to every part and thinned per role - bass keeps only the lowest note (optionally re-chosen, e.g. D under the last chord), pad keeps the upper three notes tightened by dropping the top note an octave, an FM arpeggio built on the note set that fits all chords (root-4th-5th-octave such as D-G-A-D), a second pad built from major/minor seconds that move by semitone (B->C, E->F) as a contrast to the third-based pad, a melody using those guide tones with anticipations into each chord plus the all-chord tones (G, A) as connectors, an octave-lower double on a different timbre, and long-attack reverb swells on the universal tones",
 "Generate enough material for a whole ambient piece from one progression, with every layer harmonically safe. Delta vs harmony cluster (one chord tone per instrument, alternating seconds/thirds rule, meta-chord loop): a concrete derivation workflow - copy-and-thin one progression clip per role, search for a tone set common to all chords to drive arpeggio/swells, contrast a seconds-based dyad pad with the thirds-based pad, and write an anticipation melody from per-chord guide tones.",
 ["A piano roll / MIDI clips","Instruments for bass, pad, FM arp, mallet/dyad pad, lead and a long-attack swell synth"],
 [("progression","midi","2-4 chords, long sustained (e.g. 1 bar each over 4 bars)",True),("key_or_center","string","Tonal centre, or none if using parallel chords",False),("tempo_bpm","number","Slow, e.g. 70-90",False)],
 [("layers","midi","Bass, pad, arpeggio, seconds-dyad pad, melody, octave double and swell clips derived from the progression"),("common_tones","string","Notes that fit every chord, used for arp/swells/connectors")],
 ["Steady pitch: no pitch-bend swoops on swells, no randomised notes; the arpeggio is a fixed repeating pattern (Matt's preference).","Skip the transcript's beat-repeat/granulator stutter copy of the mallet part (rapid clicking texture Matt dislikes); if a texture copy is wanted use a long-grain, low-density smear instead.","The octave double may be slightly loose in timing, but must stay in tune.","Chord names (Cmaj7, Gmaj7, Bbmaj7, Fmaj7) are the transcript's example; recreate as MIDI, no copyrighted melody is reproduced.",EARLY,ABL],
 [("Write the progression: build one chord shape (e.g. maj7 = root, +4, +3, +4 semitones) and move it in parallel to new roots (C, G, Bb, F), one long sustained chord per bar, 4 bars; or use any diatonic progression.","Piano roll","Harmonic clip"),
  ("Copy the clip to a bass track and delete everything except the lowest note; try alternative bass notes under a chord (e.g. D under Fmaj7) and keep the ones that sound good.","Piano roll","Solid root/alt-bass layer"),
  ("Copy the clip to a pad (e.g. choir/voice pad) and delete the bass note so the upper three notes remain; move the highest note down an octave so voices move by small intervals rather than jumping fourths/fifths, then raise the whole pad an octave if needed for register.","Piano roll","Tight, smooth upper pad"),
  ("Find the common-tone set: test a note (and its 4th and 5th, e.g. D-G-A) against all chords; keep the set that fits every chord. Program an FM-keys arpeggio as root-4th-5th-octave (or step pattern 4-1-4) on that set, looping unchanged across the progression.","MIDI clip","Arpeggio that never clashes"),
  ("Build a seconds-based dyad pad: pick a chord tone of chord 1 (e.g. B) and move it by a semitone to the next chord's tone (C), similarly E->F; add a third below or above to form two-note intervals and play as a slow dyad trill on a mallet/vibraphone sound.","MIDI clip","Second-based layer contrasting the third-based pad"),
  ("Write the melody from per-chord guide tones (e.g. E/B over bars 1-2, F/C over bars 3-4), arriving on the next chord's tone slightly before the downbeat (anticipation), and use the common tones (G, A) as connecting notes.","MIDI clip","Steady melody that leans into each change"),
  ("Double the melody an octave lower on a contrasting synth timbre; slight timing looseness is fine.","Arrangement","Orchestral-style double, call/response option"),
  ("Add swells: a synth with a long attack and heavy reverb playing the common tones (G, A) a few times across the section, no pitch bend.","Arrangement","Performative swells that cannot clash"),
  ("Collect all clips; arrange by muting/unmuting layers per section (e.g. pad drops out leaving the dyad layer).","Arrangement","Material for a full ambient piece")],
 ["Every derived clip uses only notes from the progression clip or the verified common-tone set.","Pad voice moves between chords are mostly steps or thirds, no fourth/fifth jumps in the top voice.","Melody contains at least one anticipation per chord change.","Arpeggio and swell notes fit all chords (no audible clash when soloed with each chord)."],
 ["harmony","layers","ambient","arpeggio","common-tones","voice-leading","melody","parallel-harmony"])

S("TfBMKlJV96U","How I Make Ambient Music That Moves",
 "ambient-home-base-step-away-and-return-progression-static-sequence-anchor-expanding-harmonic-distance-stay-in-key-delayed-echo-copy",
 "Give a texture-based ambient piece direction without letting it wander: a small, steady home-base sequence (one note or a two-voice figure, unaffected by the chords, modulated only in timbre) as the tonal centre, then a piano progression that leaves the home chord and returns, each excursion going a little further (I -> near chord -> I; I -> further diatonic chord -> I; ...) while staying in one key, with an optional slightly late echo copy of the piano for interest instead of more chords or a key change",
 "Make ambient music feel like it is going somewhere while staying functional background music. Delta vs arrangement-ambient cluster (bar maps, section templates, sleep descents): a harmonic-narrative rule - establish home, expand-and-return with gradually growing harmonic distance in-key, avoid key changes because they demand attention; movement in sound (filters, LFOs) is not movement in music.",
 ["A synth for the home-base sequence","A piano/keys instrument","A delay (optional)"],
 [("key","string","One key for the whole piece",True),("home_figure","midi","1-2 note sequence on the tonic",True),("tempo_bpm","number","Slow",False)],
 [("home_layer","midi","Steady tonic sequence running the whole piece"),("excursion_progression","midi","Chord path away from and back to the home chord with increasing distance"),("arrangement_map","json","Section list with excursion distance per section")],
 ["Stay in one key: in this ambient/background function, a key change pulls attention; nearby diatonic chords = 'another room in the same house'. Use a distant key only as a rare deliberate event.","The home-base sequence keeps steady pitch; movement comes only from timbre (filter, thickness, light drive), not pitch wobble (Matt's preference).","The echo copy is a delayed duplicate of the piano line (a few tens of ms to an eighth late), not randomised or stuttered; no rapid repeats.",EARLY,"Ableton/MIDI-friendly: home layer and progression are MIDI clips; distance plan is a simple list."],
 [("Write the home base: a 1-2 voice sequence on the tonic that repeats for the whole piece; give it gentle timbre motion (slow filter/thickness changes), optionally a dry tone with no reverb.","Synth + MIDI clip","Clear tonal centre that hovers"),
  ("Rank the diatonic chords in the key by distance from the home chord (e.g. in C major: Am, Em/F nearest, then Dm/G, then Bdim/borrowed chords furthest).","Planning","Distance ladder"),
  ("Write the piano part as excursions: home -> nearest chord -> home; then home -> a slightly further chord (or two-step path) -> home; repeat, each time going a little further, taking time on each chord.","Piano roll","Expand-and-return progression in one key"),
  ("Keep the home layer playing unchanged under every excursion so each return feels like arriving back.","Arrangement","Sense of departure and return"),
  ("Add interest to the piano line instead of adding chords or changing key: duplicate it to a delayed/processed echo track set slightly late (a fixed offset), mixed under the dry piano.","Delay / MIDI offset","Extra depth, harmony unchanged"),
  ("Map sections by excursion distance (intro: home only; then excursions growing; final return home and thin out).","Arrangement","Directional ambient form")],
 ["The whole piece stays in one key (no out-of-key chords unless planned as a single event).","Each excursion returns to the home chord; the maximum distance increases across the first half.","Home-base layer MIDI is identical throughout."],
 ["arrangement","ambient","harmonic-motion","form","tonal-center","progression","background-music"])

S("rK0pEiBYfq8","Arturia Pigments: Building Evolving Pads (With Modal Synthesis)",
 "friction-excited-modal-resonator-pad-string-beam-profile-harmonic-warp-low-partials-pinned-slow-lfo-partial-limited-wavetable-bed-serial-comb-keytracked-brilliance-washed-insert-shimmer",
 "Evolving modal-synthesis pad: a sustained friction (continuous noise) exciter, optionally mixed with a soft collision impulse, drives a modal resonator bank (string profile for harmonic, beam for metallic); slight detune for width; harmonic 'warp' pushes partials up or down while the first 1-8 partials stay pinned so the fundamental holds; a slow LFO on warp (with per-voice LFO-rate offsets) for movement; longer partial ring time to blur impacts into a continuous string; a second partial-limited wavetable/additive bed underneath with an envelope opening the partial count; serial comb filter (low damping) into a master low-pass; key-tracked brilliance and level so low notes are darker; a slow pad envelope and reverb/shimmer on inserts for a fully washed sound",
 "Design a sustained, otherworldly ambient pad from resonators rather than oscillators. Delta vs physical-modeling cluster (bowed comb string, Karplus pluck, modal partial-bank voice, scale-locked resonator bank, struck strings): sustained friction excitation as a pad, partial warp with pinned low partials and slow LFO, layering with a partial-limited wavetable bed, serial comb + LP and key-tracked brilliance.",
 ["A modal/resonator synth or resonator bank (any DAW, Web Audio biquad bank)","A wavetable or additive oscillator","Comb filter, low-pass filter, reverb"],
 [("key","string","Key of the chords",True),("chords","midi","Sustained pad chords",True),("profile","string","string (harmonic) or beam (metallic)",False)],
 [("patch_recipe","json","Exciter, resonator, warp, LFO, bed, filter and FX settings"),("pad_audio","audio","Rendered evolving modal pad")],
 ["Steady pitch: the transcript's slow pitch-modulation chorus and pitch-shifting delay are omitted (Matt dislikes wobbly pitch); movement comes from partial warp, comb and filter only.","Friction exciter density kept smooth/continuous; avoid low-density settings that produce audible ticking (rapid clicking texture Matt dislikes).","Per-voice randomness applies only to timbre (density/LFO rate), never pitch.","Pinned low partials keep the fundamental stable while upper partials move.",EARLY,"Ableton/MIDI-friendly: plays any MIDI chord clip; Web Audio mapping = noise source -> parallel high-Q bandpass bank at partial ratios -> comb (feedback delay) -> lowpass."],
 [("Exciter: set a continuous friction source (filtered noise held for the note); optionally blend a soft collision impulse for a gentle attack.","Resonator synth","Sustained excitation"),
  ("Resonator: choose a string profile (harmonic partials) or beam (metallic); detune a second resonator slightly for width; lengthen the ring/decay so impacts blur into a continuous string.","Resonator synth","Continuous resonant tone"),
  ("Warp: shift partials upward (brighter, thinner middle) or downward (condensed); pin partials 1-2 (up to 8) so the fundamental stays put.","Resonator synth","Shaped spectrum with stable root"),
  ("Movement: a slow LFO on warp; give each voice a small LFO-rate offset so voices do not move in sync.","Modulation","Organic, slow spectral drift"),
  ("Bed: add a second oscillator (wavetable/additive) with partial count limited (acts like a filter) and an envelope slowly opening the partials; mix lower than the modal layer.","Oscillator 2","Fuller body underneath"),
  ("Filters: route serial into a comb filter with low damping (longer ringing) partially wet, then a master low-pass.","Filter","Resonant, focused tone"),
  ("Key-track brilliance and level on the modal layer so lower notes are darker/quieter and higher notes brighter/louder; set the pad amp envelope slow.","Keytracking","Balanced across range"),
  ("FX: reverb/shimmer and delay on inserts at high wet to wash the sound out; light compression as a leveller.","FX","Washed ambient evolving pad")],
 ["Fundamental pitch measured stable (no pitch LFO) across a 20 s held chord.","Spectral centroid moves slowly over time (warp LFO active).","Low notes render darker than high notes (key-tracked brilliance)."],
 ["pad","modal-synthesis","resonator","physical-modeling","evolving","ambient","comb-filter","keytracking"])
